---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
    title="Pilot · Sanctum Family Pass v1.0"
    description="Join the Sanctum Family Pass v1.0 pilot — a small founder cohort installing the first shipped version on their own haus."
>
    <main>
        <p class="tagline">Founder beta · spring 2026</p>

        <h1>Join the Family Pass v1.0 pilot</h1>

        <p class="lede">
            We're piloting Sanctum Family Pass v1.0 with a small number of
            technical-friend haushelds. The pilot is free. We ask for
            roughly thirty minutes of your time on first install, plus
            weekly feedback in a shared Signal group while v1 is in
            stabilization.
        </p>

        <h2>What you'll be installing</h2>
        <p>
            Sanctum Family Pass v1.0 is the first version we feel
            comfortable putting on someone else's hardware. It includes
            Sanctum Core (the open-source council, the cathedral, Force
            Flow, Living Force self-healing) plus the Screen Time module —
            the part that has been running on my own teenager for fourteen
            months without an Apple-Family-style flake-out.
        </p>
        <p>
            See <a href="/family-pass/">what's in v1</a> for the full
            list, and <a href="/install/">install</a> for the short version
            of the six-step install.
        </p>

        <h2>What we need from you</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>
                A Mac with Apple Silicon, at least 16 GB of RAM, macOS 14
                or newer. The Mac will be running Lima continuously, so
                please assume it lives in a closet or on a shelf, not on
                your work desk.
            </li>
            <li>
                A Firewalla on your LAN — Gold, Purple, or Gold Pro. Any
                generation, any firmware in the last twelve months. You
                don't need to pair it with Sanctum yet; the installer
                walks you through that.
            </li>
            <li>
                An Anthropic API key of your own (optional, only for the
                Cilghal helper). Sanctum brings its own local cathedral;
                this is purely the "do you want the cloud round-trip as a
                fallback" question.
            </li>
            <li>
                Willingness to file a Signal message when something
                breaks, and patience for "I'll have a fix tonight" on
                weekdays.
            </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>What you get</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>A working v1.0 install on your own haus, free.</li>
            <li>
                Direct access to me in a small group Signal channel for
                the duration of the pilot.
            </li>
            <li>
                A free Family Pass v1.0 lifetime license when v1.1 ships
                Stripe checkout. No upsells, no time-bombed trials.
            </li>
            <li>
                Credit in the launch notes (optional — say so on the form
                if you prefer to stay anonymous).
            </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>What this is not</h2>
        <p>
            This is not a beta-test program for a future SaaS. The
            open-source core is and will remain FSL-1.1-MIT. The Family
            Pass is a one-time license, no subscription. If we ever ship a
            paid Cloud Sync addon, it will be additive and optional. You
            are not test-driving a future paywall.
        </p>

        <hr />

        <h2>Sign up</h2>
        <p class="muted">
            Three minutes of form-filling. Replies inside 48 hours. The
            cohort is small on purpose — we want to actually answer
            everyone.
        </p>

        <iframe
            src="https://tally.so/embed/YOUR_TALLY_FORM_ID?alignLeft=1&hideTitle=1&transparentBackground=1"
            width="100%"
            height="500"
            frameborder="0"
            title="Sanctum Family Pass pilot signup form"
        ></iframe>
    </main>
</Base>
